# Normalize every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the default) writes
# CRLF, and `bun run lint` then fails on all 42 frontend source files with
# format errors that do not exist on Linux — biome.json declares
# "lineEnding": "lf". The factory validates on Linux and passes; a human
# running the same gate on Windows sees 42 phantom failures. Same command,
# different verdict, which is exactly the kind of gate you cannot trust.
#
# Git already stores LF in the object database, so this changes only what gets
# written to disk. Run `git add --renormalize .` after editing this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by the rule above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Force LF on shell scripts and Dockerfile so they work on Linux when this
# repo is checked out on Windows. These are now redundant with the blanket
# rule above, but kept explicit because breaking them breaks the VPS.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# systemd unit files are parsed by systemd on the Linux host; CRLF causes
# "Failed to parse" at install time.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
